{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088168-faerie-longevity-for-c20-changelings","id":1088168,"title":"Faerie Longevity for C20 Changelings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-05T03:07:14-07:00","id":1088168,"title":"Faerie Longevity for C20 Changelings","content":"Let's review a subject much dear to my heart, namely PC coming as close to immortality as possible, under the C20 lens. Let's assume we have a few characters that come to the conclusion the slow decay, loss, and ending of old age, Banality, and mortal death is a loathsome fate to be avoided by all means necessary (in comparison, Bedlam is still bad and to be avoided if possible, but less fearsome a fate), and this Changeling Way stuff of reincarnating in mortal bodies wasn't such a good idea after all. So by C20 conditions, this means they should:<br /> <br /> - have the Faerie Eternity Merit, which can easily extend the natural lifespan of their mortal bodies to several centuries, if they can avoid being Undone. By the way, the current writeup of the Merit states the changeling stays a childling. Since in C20 Seemings are now a reversible and switchable preferred mental/spiritual/mystical condition for changelings much more than a reflection of their physical age, this statement leaves me rather doubtful. Is this an errata to be reported, or are characters with this Merit actually meant to be locked as childlings? Also, choice of, and investment in, Arts, Merits, Birthrights, and House boons that improve bodily protection and/or grant quick recovery from real damage (e.g. Granite Skin, Huge Size, Regeneration, and/or the Tough Hide version of Animalistic Favor) seems a good idea.<br /> <br /> - spend as much time as possible in freeholds or the Dreaming. By the way, to a reading of mine, the book never explictly states staying in the Dreaming has the same anagathic effect as living in a freehold, yet it is implied to be so, and in any case what stops aging for changeling is being in proximity to concentrated sources of Glamour, and this is even more plentiful in the Dreaming (especially the Far and Deep strata) than in a freehold. Perhaps stuff for an errata? Ideally, the changeling should get some Title and join House Danann to immunize themselves to the Bedlam-inducing effects of prolonged stays in the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> - aggressively minimize their accumulation of Banality. This means to maximize the Glamour score (use Rapture or the Musing Threshold as often as possible), use Glamour (or stints in the Dreaming) to nullify any Banality temporary points they may get, pick as many quests as necessary to lower their Banality score to 1, embrace the Seeming that grants them the greatest immunity to the Banality triggers they most frequently face according to their lifestyle (depending on circumstances, all three may qualify), and avoid all other Banality triggers at all costs. By the way, from my reading of the book, I do not know if failing to enchant a mortal or killing a chimera still count as Banality triggers or not in the Dreaming, and this seems relevant to the issue. I'm rather uncertain if Poetic Heart is any worth its price in this context since it may be used very sparingly.<br /> <br /> I welcome other ideas and suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 05-05-2017, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T06:11:27-07:00","id":1088239,"title":"","content":"Back in 2e, it was stated numerous times that heavy exposure to the Dreaming can retard aging---how do you think David managed to stay so fit? (It's not like the guy was out there doing s**t personally anymore...)<br /> <br /> Plus, the Siochain. Though game mechanics for these guys were never given, the fluff indicated that a Siochain was a changeling who perfectly 'balanced' their mundane and magical lives, re-achieving genuine faerie immortality. Kind of like Kithain Golconda, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T07:30:55-07:00","id":1088277,"title":"","content":"There's a specific antagonist type, dream eaters, which are a kind of chimera. Most don't survive their first minutes or hours, because they're chimera with Banality scores, but there are rumored ancient ones that gorge on Glamour, rack up Banality, and then retreat to the Deep Dreaming until their Banality lowers again. <br /> <br /> Might be you can work something along those lines, balancing Dreaming with Autumn, to achieve it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T07:36:51-07:00","id":1088280,"title":"","content":"As I don't have it yet (and won't have it till it's released for public consumption), could someone please tell me if Siochain are still a thing? They were mentioned in 2e as being extremely powerful but....no stats were ever given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T07:56:40-07:00","id":1088287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088168-faerie-longevity-for-c20-changelings?p=1088280#post1088280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I don't have it yet (and won't have it till it's released for public consumption), could someone please tell me if Siochain are still a thing? They were mentioned in 2e as being extremely powerful but....no stats were ever given.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much like Vampire Golconda, they are mentioned, but given a semi-mythical status, with no stats, rules for achievement, or guidelines to play one. IIRC, one of the leaders of House Danann is an eshu that is heavily rumored to be a Siochain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T07:57:33-07:00","id":1088289,"title":"","content":"Ahhhh thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T08:13:49-07:00","id":1088293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088168-faerie-longevity-for-c20-changelings?p=1088239#post1088239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in 2e, it was stated numerous times that heavy exposure to the Dreaming can retard aging---how do you think David managed to stay so fit? (It's not like the guy was out there doing s**t personally anymore...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, and apparently valid in C20 as well. As far as I can tell, the main difference from 2e in this regard is prolonged exposure to the Dreaming only wipes out permanent Banality as long as you stay there - on the other hand, its shedding occurs somewhat more quickly than before. As of now, quests are the only reliable thing to shed permaNality; then again, heroic Deeds seem far from difficult to find in the Dreaming, if not exactly easy to accomplish. If one is careful never to let one's Banality score much higher than the default 3, to minimize it to 1 and keep it there seems not that overwhelmingly difficult. You only have to give up Ravaging and invoking the Autumn as reliable tools to reap Glamour or protect oneself from chimerical threats.<br /> <br /> Broadly speaking, Arcadian Sidhe (and other characters with the nasty Flaw that duplicates their Frailty) seem the worst characters possible to purse faerie longevity, because of their high vulnerability to Banality. Then again, they change Frailty once they go into the Dreaming, and being High King, David in all likelihood has such a privileged access to changeling resources that he can make up for the difference even if he stays in earthly freeholds all the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, the Siochain. Though game mechanics for these guys were never given, the fluff indicated that a Siochain was a changeling who perfectly 'balanced' their mundane and magical lives, re-achieving genuine faerie immortality. Kind of like Kithain Golconda, really. </div> </div> </div>True. On the other hand, just like Golconda, the very fuzzy state of Siochain-hood makes it rather difficult to plan and make it a serious long-term character objective, unlike say becoming an Archmage or an Incarnate Beast in CoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 05-05-2017, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T16:25:42-07:00","id":1088543,"title":"","content":"Step One: Find a Vampire. Step Two: have said vampire remove all your blood. Step Three: Have vampire add one pint of its blood into your body. Step Four: Become a Maeghar!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}